<%# "How to know it's really BonID" — like login.gov's "Here's how you
    know", but BonID is not a government site, so it explains how to spot
    the real BonID (address, code sender, never share the code).
    Native <details>: works without JavaScript.
    The address comes from the configured base URL (BONID_BASE_URL;
    bonid.ngrok.app in dev), never from the request: a copy of the site
    must not be able to "confirm" its own address. %>
<% official_host = URI.parse(Rails.configuration.bonid_base_url.to_s).host.presence || "verifyem.ht" rescue "verifyem.ht" %>
<details class="auth-how-to-know">
  <summary>
    <i class="ri-shield-check-line" aria-hidden="true"></i>
    <%= t("citizen_portal.auth.how_to_know.summary") %>
    <i class="ri-arrow-down-s-line auth-how-to-know__chevron" aria-hidden="true"></i>
  </summary>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <i class="ri-lock-line" aria-hidden="true"></i>
      <span><%= t("citizen_portal.auth.how_to_know.address_html", host: official_host) %></span>
    </li>
    <li>
      <i class="ri-mail-check-line" aria-hidden="true"></i>
      <span><%= t("citizen_portal.auth.how_to_know.sender_html") %></span>
    </li>
    <li>
      <i class="ri-chat-off-line" aria-hidden="true"></i>
      <span><%= t("citizen_portal.auth.how_to_know.never_share") %></span>
    </li>
  </ul>
</details>
